# 3. BUDGET PAGE

This page is your strongest screen.

---

## Monthly Spending Goal

This is:

```text
monthly budget
```

Example:

```text
₦300,000
```

Current goal tag:

Means:

```text
active budget plan
```

---

## Remaining Balance

Formula:

```text
budget - spent
```

Example:

```text
300k - 180k
= ₦120k
```

---

## "You can spend X/day"

Very important metric.

Formula:

```text
remaining balance ÷ days left
```

Example:

```text
120,000 ÷ 9
= ₦13,333/day
```

This is powerful because it guides behavior.

User immediately knows:

> “If I spend above ₦13k/day, I may overspend.”

This is premium-fintech behavior.

---

## Spending Health Section

You asked how to compute this.

This should represent:

### budget health score

Formula:

```text
spent ÷ expected spending pace
```

Here’s the smarter approach:

Expected spending by today:

Formula:

```text
(currentDay ÷ daysInMonth)
× budget
```

Example:

Day 22 of 31:

Expected:

```text
22 ÷ 31 × 300k

= ₦212,903
```

Actual spent:

```text
₦180k
```

User is BELOW pace.

Healthy.

Health %:

```text
180k ÷ 212k × 100
= 84%
```

Meaning:

```text
84% of expected spending pace
```

Progress bar:

### Rules

```text

```

This becomes meaningful UX.

Not fake percentages.

---

## Category Budgets

Each category has:

```text
allocated amount
```

Example:

```text
Food Budget = ₦60k
```

Spent:

```text
₦51k
```

Formula:

```text
spent ÷ category budget × 100
```

Example:

```text
51k ÷ 60k
= 85%
```

Display:

```text
Food & Dining

85% used
₦51,000 of ₦60,000
```

Example over budget:

Shopping:

```text
Budget: ₦30k
Spent: ₦35k
```

Display:

```text
117% used
₦35,000 of ₦30,000
```

Progress bar red.

