# Why you faced this challenge

Because you skipped:

```text
Data architecture
```

You started from:

```text
UI → logic
```

Instead of:

```text
financial model → logic → UI
```

Professional apps start with:

### Entity model

Example:

```dart
Expense
Budget
Category
Transaction
Savings
```

Then:

### computed values

Then:

### UI

That’s why fintech apps feel “connected.”

Everything derives from one source of truth.

## What you should do next

Before writing more UI:

Create a file:

```text
finance_calculator.dart
```

Put ALL formulas there.

Example:

```dart
double calculateAmountLeft(
  double budget,
  double spent,
) {
  return budget - spent;
}
```

Your widgets should display computed data, not hardcoded math.

That one architectural decision will make Spendly feel like a real product instead of a UI demo.
